  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening African Maritime Security Institutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhance maritime security and governance in developing, fragile and conflict-prone African countries through active dissemination of research results, technical support and capacity building, targeted advice to policy and decision makers and the establishment of a Maritime Strategic Support Group (MSSG) at the AU level. The Project&#x2019;s expected effect(s) on society is/are to equip decision-makers with the research advice, capacity and tools required to combat identified maritime crimes and security threats and enhance maritime security and governance in developing, fragile and conflict-prone African countries. The expected effects for the target group of the Project are that African maritime policy and practice strengthened and promoted by evidence-based research and security and governance activities in the field of maritime security and crime.</narrative>
  </description>
